    "result_text": "The build is green: **59 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `BusinessDay.java` to skip public holidays as well as weekends.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/BusinessDay.java`):\n- Added a fixed `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Added an `isBusinessDay` helper that treats Saturdays, Sundays, and any listed holiday as non-business.\n- Rewrote `rollForward` from a fixed weekend-only jump to a loop that advances one day at a time until it lands on a non-holiday weekday.\n\nThe loop-based approach correctly handles chained cases \u2014 e.g. `2026-12-25` (Fri holiday) \u2192 skips Sat/Sun \u2192 `2026-12-28` (also a holiday) \u2192 rolls forward to `2026-12-29`.\n\nThe change is confined to `rollForward`, so `effective(...)` and its caller `BuildOwner` pick up the new behavior automatically. The new `Cp47Tests` (holiday-business-day invariant) and all existing tests pass.",
